# `signal::bartlett`

## Signature

```cpp
pluss::Series signal::bartlett(
    std::int64_t size,
    const signal::WindowOptions& options = {});
```

## What It Does

Creates a triangular Bartlett taper. In symmetric mode, ordinary lengths greater than one reach zero at both endpoints and peak near the center.

## Parameters

`size`
: Number of coefficients to return. Zero returns an empty rank-one `Series`; one returns the mathematically useful singleton coefficient.

`options`
: Endpoint, dtype, and platform policy. Bartlett is a piecewise-linear taper. It suppresses leakage more than `boxcar` while broadening the main spectral lobe.

## Returns

A rank-one floating `Series` of length `size`, allocated with the requested dtype and platform.

## Errors

Rejects a negative `size`, a non-floating dtype, or an unsupported platform request.

